WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.729
Speaker 1: Ladies and gentlemen, it's time
for the Friday mailbag.

00:00:02.729 --> 00:00:05.870
You can email in to info at David Pakman dot
com.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:11.139
Sometimes in addition to emails will feature
a tweet, a Facebook message, a YouTube comment.

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:12.139
Something else.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:14.900
And I want to start today with a Facebook
message.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.910
And one of the things every once in a while
I try to do, it's a very dangerous thing to

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.170
do, is a very fraught thing to do.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.070
I will try to engage with a troll or just
a nut.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.200
And last time I did this, it was an anti-vax
person.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.270
And I actually said, hey, let's let's talk
to them, let's figure out how they came to

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.780
believe, the things they believe.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:40.940
And I asked some questions and it was all
very weird and it went nowhere and we learned

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.940
very little.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.950
I tried again the other day.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.470
This is someone that send sending a message
via Facebook.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:51.960
Stanley said, We found fraud attached to you.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.250
You need to come clean with your listeners
about your scam.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.910
So I wrote back, Great.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.440
Please send the information of fraud and we
will come clean.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.820
No idea what you're talking about offhand.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:11.770
So they write back and they say, I'm sending
it to the faculty license department.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.770
What's that?

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.020
And then they said the FCC department.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.220
To which I explained again, this is an experiment
to see where it goes.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.360
I said, We aren't governed by the FCC.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.729
The FCC doesn't govern the Internet.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:26.590
Let us know the fraud so that we can investigate.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.740
To which Stanley said, Yes, you are.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:35.740
You're of course it's the wrong your your
broadcasting which fall in FCC regulations

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.220
and you're wrong.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:44.840
You're a subscriber channel as well, which
falls into money's changing hands.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.140
And I said, money's changing.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.530
Hands is under the purview of the FTC, not
the FCC.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.820
Can you let us know the fraud so we can investigate
and correct it?

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.240
To which I never heard back.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:04.159
So another exercise in the futility of trying
to substantively engage with the trolls.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:05.159
Next.

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:07.619
The email is from Patrick.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:10.220
Patrick is very angry with me.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.220
Patrick says, Hi, David.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.730
